When I try to run the example code ESP32 > Camera > CameraWebServer it runs perfectly on my ESP32-CAM when choosing

`#define CAMERA_MODEL_AI_THINKER`

But you seem to have changed some lines of code in the setup, to run it in softAP mode. When I replace the wifi-code in the setup with

```
  WiFi.setHostname("ESP32_CAM");
  delay(500);

  // Start AP mode
  WiFi.softAP(ssid, password);

  startCameraServer();

  Serial.print("Camera Ready! Use 'http://");
  Serial.println(WiFi.softAPIP());
  Serial.println("' to connect");
```
it runs perfectly on 25 fps. I am running esp32 version 1.0.4 and using the module ESP32-CAM-MB.

Please notice that I removed following line of code:
`  WiFi.begin(ssid, password);`
as this is not necessary when running in softAP-mode.

But when I insert the line, in order to reproduce your problem, I indeed notice freezing issues, althoug not as bad as yours.
